    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d392">

                <pb facs="0436" n="402" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg402"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Romero to Mr. Sherman.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Mexico</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-09-23"><hi rendition="#italic">September 23,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have had the honor to receive
                    your note, No. 288, bearing date of yesterday, in reply to that which, in
                    obedience to the instructions of the Government of Mexico, I addressed to you on
                    the 9th ultimo, proposing the negotiation of a convention for the purpose of
                    rectifying the demarcation of the boundary line between Mexico and the United
                    States in accordance with the treaty of December 30, 1853, between the Rio
                    Grande (monument No. 1) and the Colorado River (monument No. 205) or throughout
                    its extent if this should be preferred by the United States Government.</p>
                <p>You were pleased to state, in your aforesaid note, the objections which the
                    United States Government has to accepting the proposition of the Mexican
                    Government, and in order that the latter Government may be enabled to examine
                    them properly, I shall send it a copy of your note without delay.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">M. Romero.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
